sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Analyst
  participant UI as React UI
  participant API as Secure API
  participant W as Durable Workflow
  participant D as Data Catalog
  participant PY as Primary Python
  participant R as Independent R
  participant S as Scientific QA
  participant E as Official Evidence
  participant AI as AI Gateway
  participant C as Claim Compiler
  participant G as Release Gate
  participant H as Human Reviewer
  Analyst->>UI: define district and investigation question
  UI->>API: POST investigation with idempotency key
  API->>W: authorize and start versioned run
  W->>D: pin licensed data and indicator contract
  par independent science
    W->>PY: compute estimates and SE
    PY-->>S: computed inputs and results
  and reference science
    W->>R: independently compute estimates and SE
    R-->>S: independent results and provenance
  end
  S->>S: reconcile with registered tolerances
  alt scientific failure
    S-->>W: scientific validation failed
    W-->>UI: restricted draft with defect
  else science validated
    W->>E: independently fetch and compare official facts
    alt source unavailable
      E-->>W: retrieval failed or hash verified cache result
    else source available
      E-->>W: comparable verified references or conflicts
    end
    W->>AI: provide suppression checked aggregate evidence
    AI-->>W: typed claim proposals and hypotheses
    W->>C: validate claim IDs and deterministic rendering
    C-->>G: frozen report version and checks
    alt failed gate
      G-->>UI: restricted draft with reasons
    else eligible for review
      G->>H: request authorized review
      alt approved
        H->>G: signed approval
        G-->>UI: approved version and authorized exports
      else rejected
        H-->>UI: review required and evidence gaps
      end
    end
  end
